<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<RootNamespace>Assimalign.Cohesion.Web.Cors</RootNamespace>
		<Description>Cross-origin resource sharing for the Cohesion Web pipeline, per the Fetch standard's CORS protocol. UseCors answers CORS preflights (204 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin, -Methods, -Headers, -Credentials and -Max-Age, or no CORS headers at all when the policy denies the request) and stamps actual responses with the allowed origin, credentials and exposed headers, plus Vary: Origin whenever the answer depends on the origin. Policies are immutable and validated when built: origins must be serialized origins (exact list, any origin, or an AOT-safe predicate), any-origin cannot carry credentials, and methods and request headers follow Fetch matching (byte-case-sensitive methods with the CORS-safelisted ones always allowed, case-insensitive header names). Policies are selected per endpoint from sealed routing metadata (RequireCors, DisableCors) published by UseRouting, falling back to a default policy.</Description>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Web" />
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Web.Routing" />
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Http" />
		<CohesionProjectReference Include="Assimalign.Cohesion.Http.Streaming" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
